Each node: "id" (any string), "speaker" (a cast id), "line" (the spoken line), and "options": exactly 4 — one of EACH hidden kind:
- "safe": assert a G LIMPsed fact at its exact true value. Set "fact" to a glimpsed fact id and "value" to its true value verbatim. Works if the player knows it. works_if: [{"glimpsed": fact}]. doubt_on_success 0, doubt_on_fail 1.
- "deflect": a vague non-answer or turn it back. NO fact, NO value. works_if: [{"vague_streak_lt": 2}] or [{"target_personality": "..."}] or [{"target": cast_id}]. doubt_on_fail 1.
- "overreach": confidently assert a detail from an UNKNOWN (non-glimpsed) fact. Set "fact" to a non-glimpsed fact id and "value" to a plausible claim. This buys credibility now but a LATER observer calls it in. doubt_on_success -1 (the only move that can lower doubt), doubt_on_fail 2. works_if: [] or [{"turn_lt": n}].
- "reinforce": restate or stand by something already claimed. Set "fact" to a fact id and "value" to the SAME value you gave before. works_if: [{"claimed": fact}]. doubt_on_fail 1.
Each option also: "tag" (from the tag list), "text" (player voice, max 160 chars), "line_if_pass", "line_if_fail", "rationale" (one sentence, review only).

"works_if" is ALWAYS a JSON LIST of 0-2 condition atoms (use [] when ungated), never a single object. Atoms (use ONLY these): {"glimpsed": fact_id} {"claimed": fact_id} {"not_claimed": fact_id} {"target": cast_id} {"target_personality": "curious|skeptical|narcissist|formal|hostile"} {"turn_lt": n} {"doubt_lt": n} {"vague_streak_lt": n}

Rules:
- Do NOT include "next" — the engine chains the nodes.
- The working kind must VARY across the conversation: no kind should be the winning one every turn; deflect/reinforce need conditions that are sometimes false.
- A "safe" fact MUST be glimpsed; an "overreach" fact MUST NOT be glimpsed. Getting this wrong fails validation.
- Adult, fictional social setting. Same content bans as before.
